---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import NewsletterCTA from '../components/NewsletterCTA.astro';
const values = [
  ['01','This is personal to us.','A close family member lives with celiac disease, and Amaya and her mom navigate gluten sensitivity. Our gluten-free focus began at our own family table and guides the food we are developing.'],
  ['02','Care goes into the process.','We are especially cautious about cross-contact. Our ingredient sourcing, separate storage, equipment, and preparation practices are being built around our gluten-free focus. Those are the standards our celiac family member relies on at our own table. We are not yet certified, and we will share the finished process clearly without claiming certification until it is in place.'],
  ['03','Simple, all-natural ingredients.','Our development recipes are all natural and made without silicones, parabens, or gums. We’ll share complete ingredients, applicable allergens, and product details before confirming an order. Gluten-free does not mean free from every other allergen.'],
  ['04','Small beginnings. Shared values.','A father–daughter partnership in Haymarket, Virginia. We want to meet the people who enjoy our food, listen to their feedback, and grow at a pace that keeps our family’s care at the center.'],
];
---
<Layout title="Our Approach" description="How Two Spoons is building a thoughtful gluten-free pantry: food-first recipes, clear ingredients, and the care of a family business."><div class="container"><header class="page-intro"><span class="eyebrow">A LITTLE CARE GOES A LONG WAY</span><h1>Good things take<br/><em>thoughtful ingredients.</em></h1><p>And by ingredients, we mean the care, curiosity, and honesty that go into building this little family business.</p></header><div class="approach-grid">{values.map(([n,title,body])=><article class="approach-card"><span class="number">{n}<span aria-hidden="true">.</span></span><h2>{title}</h2><p>{body}</p></article>)}</div><div class="notice"><Icon name="leaf"/><div><strong>A note about our gluten-free focus</strong><p>We’re still in development and do not claim third-party gluten-free certification or suitability for every dietary need. Final product information will be available before any order is confirmed. Please review that information when deciding what’s right for you.</p></div></div><section class="faq-section"><h2>Let’s keep it <em>clear.</em></h2><details class="faq"><summary>Are your products certified gluten-free?</summary><p>We do not currently claim third-party certification. Gluten-free is the focus of our product development. We’ll share the details of our sourcing, process, and finished products as we prepare to launch.</p></details><details class="faq"><summary>Are your products nut-free, dairy-free, or vegan?</summary><p>We haven’t finalized recipes or allergen declarations yet, so we can’t make those claims. Complete ingredients and applicable allergens will be provided for each finished product before order confirmation.</p></details><details class="faq"><summary>What does “small batch” mean to you?</summary><p>Our plan is to make modest quantities in a home kitchen, learn from each batch, and grow carefully. We’re building a small initial range rather than a large catalog.</p></details><details class="faq"><summary>Can I ask about a dietary requirement?</summary><p>Of course. <a href="/contact">Send us a note</a> about what you’re looking for. We’ll answer honestly about what’s decided and what’s still in development. Please don’t include private medical information.</p></details></section></div><NewsletterCTA/></Layout>
